{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"selasi-and-the-five-drums","version":1,"title":"Selasi and the Five Drums","ageTiers":["3-4","5-6"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Selasi loved the sound of drums. Boom, boom, boom! She wanted to play too.","sentences":["Selasi loved the sound of drums.","Boom, boom, boom!","She wanted to play too."],"image":"sha256:40334c907b0750660d914b6d98670216e9d51e791cd72873632f9c9949ab4779","alt":"A smiling girl in a yellow dress taps her hands to a beat in a sunny yard.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:1d8d157e50385ab634ddab45e3feb9362ef0866da9da8e10f2bc89c55baa473d","durationMs":7640,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3007],[3007,5688],[5688,7640]],"words":[[0,488],[488,894],[894,1138],[1138,1544],[1544,1707],[1707,3007],[3007,3738],[3738,4469],[4469,5688],[5688,5932],[5932,6420],[6420,6583],[6583,6908],[6908,7640]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"In the yard sat five drums. Selasi counted them. One, two, three, four, five!","sentences":["In the yard sat five drums.","Selasi counted them.","One, two, three, four, five!"],"image":"sha256:e960278a45de47078b258c932fda61d188b72739c91ad90f5bf6b97ef763c78b","alt":"Five drums stand in a row on swept earth while the girl points at each in turn.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:3cd8a31473b0f4111429a014ae324b68e714530d3af08158a22c890285e0b70d","durationMs":10760,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3279],[3279,6148],[6148,10760]],"words":[[0,205],[205,512],[512,922],[922,1229],[1229,1639],[1639,3279],[3279,3894],[3894,4611],[4611,6148],[6148,6968],[6968,7788],[7788,8813],[8813,9735],[9735,10760]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"Her big brother Mawuli took one drum. Aunty Esinam took one drum. Now three drums were left.","sentences":["Her big brother Mawuli took one drum.","Aunty Esinam took one drum.","Now three drums were left."],"image":"sha256:17fe77c01e2f37231034127cc00b2ef2891946b9fe2e928c433f62e5fba7c235","alt":"A boy and a young woman each pick up a drum, leaving three drums on the ground.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:94765ffebd7ff7140887c47e30d01e914f5a771078c586a2b837e771fcb1d5f8","durationMs":9720,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3947],[3947,7123],[7123,9720]],"words":[[0,289],[289,578],[578,1252],[1252,1829],[1829,2214],[2214,2503],[2503,3947],[3947,4428],[4428,5005],[5005,5390],[5390,5679],[5679,7123],[7123,7412],[7412,7893],[7893,8374],[8374,8759],[8759,9720]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Senyo and Kafui came to play. Each friend took a drum. Now only one drum was left.","sentences":["Senyo and Kafui came to play.","Each friend took a drum.","Now only one drum was left."],"image":"sha256:d6990529d28886ebcc8a26dea9604d43dd249e9a4f227f9357ffb58110c35884","alt":"Two small friends pick up drums, leaving a single drum in the middle of the yard.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:e1ec8115906a61720471b1a06441e88cd0885d5d95e950815a0f8adcbb3d5d8d","durationMs":9320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3446],[3446,6587],[6587,9320]],"words":[[0,507],[507,811],[811,1318],[1318,1723],[1723,1926],[1926,3446],[3446,3851],[3851,4459],[4459,4864],[4864,5067],[5067,6587],[6587,6891],[6891,7296],[7296,7600],[7600,8005],[8005,8309],[8309,9320]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"Selasi reached for the last drum. But her little cousin Yawa had no drum, and Yawa looked sad.","sentences":["Selasi reached for the last drum.","But her little cousin Yawa had no drum, and Yawa looked sad."],"image":"sha256:0e9202ad63587a6708a42129b08d6b33e274cccc28c2b69840670ff73354ef3a","alt":"The girl’s hand is on the last drum while her toddler cousin stands nearby with a sad face.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:0dc84c17849f0eceb8b146b065c29abc2e2673641abc3fc5f99d498a3ad79849","durationMs":8560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3390],[3390,8560]],"words":[[0,535],[535,1159],[1159,1427],[1427,1695],[1695,2052],[2052,3390],[3390,3658],[3658,3926],[3926,4461],[4461,4996],[4996,5353],[5353,5621],[5621,5799],[5799,6602],[6602,6870],[6870,7227],[7227,7762],[7762,8560]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"Selasi gave Yawa the last drum. Then she found a big tin and two wooden spoons. Tap, tap, tap!","sentences":["Selasi gave Yawa the last drum.","Then she found a big tin and two wooden spoons.","Tap, tap, tap!"],"image":"sha256:54cade64207fe75f138ce04ce3180ed07c69e27628f7ee74aab8a3d804b610a8","alt":"The girl taps a large tin with two spoons while the toddler happily holds the last drum.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:79ec1f4e747aeef1a18b3888154a04f07b692845d4ebc91004ba5841a6aee0c1","durationMs":10640,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3482],[3482,8220],[8220,10640]],"words":[[0,580],[580,967],[967,1354],[1354,1644],[1644,2031],[2031,3482],[3482,3869],[3869,4159],[4159,4643],[4643,4836],[4836,5126],[5126,5416],[5416,5706],[5706,5996],[5996,6576],[6576,8220],[8220,8994],[8994,9768],[9768,10640]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"Now six friends played together. Boom, tap, boom, tap! One, two, three, four, five, six!","sentences":["Now six friends played together.","Boom, tap, boom, tap!","One, two, three, four, five, six!"],"image":"sha256:bdca24098471d19d1146528cea9d61c651c339c5b22c20da3d0d32274f89318f","alt":"Six people play drums and a tin together in a circle, all smiling.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:a4ce8d1a5ccc3c51369d22601cc6d6cbc0d272346318b77c39e4dc0a97cb6def","durationMs":10560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3064],[3064,6288],[6288,10560]],"words":[[0,242],[242,484],[484,1048],[1048,1532],[1532,3064],[3064,3789],[3789,4434],[4434,5159],[5159,6288],[6288,6933],[6933,7578],[7578,8384],[8384,9109],[9109,9834],[9834,10560]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"Selasi smiled. Making music together felt even better than playing alone. The end.","sentences":["Selasi smiled.","Making music together felt even better than playing alone.",